{"step_index":61,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-23T06:40:37Z","input_tokens":3144,"cache_read_tokens":55534,"output_tokens":3309,"content":"## Standards\n\n*Reviewed [ai.rs](file:///home/derek/projects/ryz/src/core/ai.rs#L1-L66) against [CONTEXT.md](file:///home/derek/projects/ryz/CONTEXT.md#L16-L19), [ADR 0002](file:///home/derek/projects/ryz/docs/adr/0002-decoupled-generic-ai-client.md), Rust idioms, and the Fowler smell baseline.*\n\n### (a) Documented Standards & Rust Idiom Violations\n\n1. **Missing Domain Types & API Contract (Hard Violation — [CONTEXT.md](file:///home/derek/projects/ryz/CONTEXT.md#L16-L19), [ADR 0002](file:///home/derek/projects/ryz/docs/adr/0002-decoupled-generic-ai-client.md#L10-L18))**\n   - [`text`](file:///home/derek/projects/ryz/src/core/ai.rs#L14-L48) is a private standalone function instead of the specified `AiClient`, `CompletionRequest`, `ChatMessage` types and `complete` / `complete_json_array` methods.\n2. **Hardcoded Endpoint, Model & `.env` Loading (Hard Violation — [ADR 0002 §4](file:///home/derek/projects/ryz/docs/adr/0002-decoupled-generic-ai-client.md#L17))**\n   - [ai.rs](file:///home/derek/projects/ryz/src/core/ai.rs#L15-L25) loads `.env` (`dotenv().ok()`), reads `OPENAI_API_KEY` from the environment, and hardcodes `with_api_base(\"https://ry953ga.abc-tunnel.us/v1\")` and `.model(\"free\")`. ADR 0002 requires accepting arbitrary `base_url`, `api_key`, and `model` configurations.\n3. **Panicking inside a `Result`-Returning Function (Hard Violation — Rust Error Idiom)**\n   - [ai.rs](file:///home/derek/projects/ryz/src/core/ai.rs#L16): `env::var(\"OPENAI_API_KEY\").expect(\"API Key not found\")` panics instead of propagating via `?`.\n4. **Non-`Send + Sync` Error Type Across Async Boundaries (Judgement Call — Rust Async Idiom)**\n   - [`text`](file:///home/derek/projects/ryz/src/core/ai.rs#L14) returns `Box<dyn Error>` (without `+ Send + Sync`), preventing background tasks from being spawned via `tokio::spawn` as required by [CONTEXT.md](file:///home/derek/projects/ryz/CONTEXT.md#L33).\n5. **Redundant `Ok(llm_response?)` Unwrap/Re-wrap (Judgement Call — Rust Idiom)**\n   - [ai.rs](file:///home/derek/projects/ryz/src/core\n<truncated 5788 bytes>\npenAIConfig,\n    types::chat::{\n        ChatCompletionRequestSystemMessageArgs, ChatCompletionRequestUserMessageArgs,\n        CreateChatCompletionRequestArgs,\n    },\n};\n\npub async fn text(system: &str, user: &str) -> Result<String, Box<dyn Error + Send + Sync>> {\n    dotenvy::dotenv().ok();\n    let api_key = env::var(\"OPENAI_API_KEY\")?;\n\n    let config = OpenAIConfig::new()\n        .with_api_key(api_key)\n        .with_api_base(\"https://ry953ga.abc-tunnel.us/v1\");\n\n    let request = CreateChatCompletionRequestArgs::default()\n        .max_tokens(512u32)\n        .model(\"free\")\n        .stream(false)\n        .messages([\n            ChatCompletionRequestSystemMessageArgs::default()\n                .content(system)\n                .build()?\n                .into(),\n            ChatCompletionRequestUserMessageArgs::default()\n                .content(user)\n                .build()?\n                .into(),\n        ])\n        .build()?;\n\n    let response = Client::with_config(config).chat().create(request).await?;\n\n    response\n        .choices\n        .into_iter()\n        .next()\n        .and_then(|choice| choice.message.content)\n        .ok_or_else(|| \"Empty response\".into())\n}\n\n#[cfg(test)]\nmod tests {\n    use super::*;\n\n    #[tokio::test]\n    async fn test_text() {\n        let result = text(\"You are a professional assistant\", \"Hello who are you\")\n            .await\n            .expect(\"API request failed\");\n\n        assert!(!result.is_empty(), \"Result should not be empty\");\n        dbg!(result);\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### What changed for readability & conciseness:\n- **Uses `system` and `user` parameters** instead of hardcoded message strings.\n- **Propagates errors with `?`** (`env::var(\"OPENAI_API_KEY\")?`) instead of panicking with `.expect(...)`.\n- **Eliminates intermediate `llm_response` variable** by returning the `Option::ok_or_else(...)` expression directly.\n- **Simplifies the unit test** with `.expect(\"API request failed\")`, which automatically prints the `Err` debug value on failure and unwraps the `String` in one step.","thinking":"Here's the refactoring of `ai.rs`:\n\nInitial examination revealed potential standards violations and discrepancies with the specified requirements, prompting further scrutiny of the codebase. Addressing these identified issues involves restructuring the code to align with established best practices and ensuring functional adherence to the defined specifications. The objective is to achieve a more maintainable and reliable implementation.\n\n\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
